## 2. Entry Points — API vs Worker

There are exactly **two entry points** and they must never share a process:

```typescript
// main.ts — API server only (Oak Application)
const app = createApp(AppMode.MAIN);
await app.listen({ port: 8000 });

// main-worker.ts — BullMQ worker only (NO Oak, NO HTTP)
const worker = createWorker(redis, processEvaluateJob, QUEUE_NAMES.WORKER_EVALUATE);
worker.on("completed", ...)
worker.on("failed", ...)
```

- API server: accepts HTTP, writes to DB, adds to queue. **Never does heavy
  processing.**
- Worker: runs as a **separate Deno process**, consumes queue, calls internal
  services, writes results back to DB.
- Separate Redis clients: `createWorkerRedisClient()` for the worker,
  `getRedisClient()` for the API server.

