## 9. Cross-Module & Cross-Layer Communication

### Rules

1. **Modules can call internal services** — this is normal and expected
2. **Modules can call other module services** — only for read operations, never
   for mutations that bypass the calling module's controller
3. **Internal services can call other internal services** — composition is
   encouraged
4. **Internal services should NOT call module services** — this creates circular
   dependencies

### Calling Internal Services from Module Service

```typescript
// modules/evaluation/evaluation.service.ts
import { coreService } from "@src/intenals/core/core.service.ts";
import { createWebService } from "@src/intenals/web/web.service.ts";

export const evaluationService = {
  // Module service is thin — just coordinates
  async preview(data: PreviewBody) {
    const webService = createWebService();
    const content = await webService.getContent(data.url);
    // ...
  },
};
```

### Calling Internal Services from Worker

```typescript
// src/main-worker.ts
import { coreService } from "@src/intenals/core/core.service.ts";
import { evaluationRepo } from "@src/modules/evaluation/evaluation.repo.ts";

const core = createCoreService();
const result = await core.processEval(url, query);
```

